SUMMARY:A Halloween Walk at the John C. Campbell Folk School in Brasstown 
 NC
DESCRIPTION:Haywood County Walking Meetup Group\nThe John C. Campbell Folk
  School is located in Brasstown\, Clay County\, NC. It has classes in over
  50 subjects\, including art\, craft\, dance\, music\, and nature. (My wif
 e took lap dulcimer lessons there many years ago. A family friend teaches 
 there regularly.) This is the place where John Jacob Niles first performed
  a song he had collected\, "I Wonder as I Wander".\n\nWe will gather in th
 e main parking lot of the campus. Our first stop will be at Keith House\, 
 where there are restrooms. We will go to the Craft Shop\, follow some trai
 ls\, visit the Herb Garden\, see the Eagle Dancer Sculpture\, and past a k
 iln. This is one walk where we will definitely not hesitate to stop and lo
 ok at various things there are to see. Your camera is a must on this one.\
 n\nOur route is 5 KM/3.1 miles. Tennis shoes are fine\, as there is no sig
 nificant elevation change. Most will not want walking sticks (although I p
 lan to take one). Bring a protein snack and plenty of water. Wheelchairs m
 ight have a somewhat hard time\, but trail strollers should be ok. If I re
 member\, dogs would probably be ok.\n\nBefore you leave\, you may want to 
 pick up lunch at the Folk School. You might bring a picnic lunch from home
 . Or you might catch some lunch after you have left campus and are on your
  way home.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/haywood-county-walking-meetup-group/e
 vents/316463898/
